This is not part of the static-removal refactor. `fips_compliant` used to read the variable with `env::var(...).ok()`, and now it uses `env::var_os(...)`. The effect: a non-UTF-8 value of `TAURI_BUNDLER_WIX_FIPS_COMPLIANT` used to fall through to `config.fips_compliant`, and now it becomes `Some(false)` because `OsString == "true"` is false. That silently overrides a config value of `true`. The change file still says "no user facing changes".

